  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.8"/>
    <code code="51848-0" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation note"/>
    <title>Assessment</title>
    <text><list><item>Uterus larger than dates in early pregnancy: 9 weeks by a certain last menstrual period, with the uterus about 12 to 13 weeks in size; nausea and vomiting heavier than in her first pregnancy; no bleeding; cause not yet known (multiple pregnancy, dating error, fibroids, or molar pregnancy): active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Nausea and vomiting of pregnancy, moderate (PUQE score 9); keeping fluids down; no weight loss or ketonuria: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Iron deficiency anemia in pregnancy: hemoglobin 10.8 g/dL, MCV 79 fL, ferritin 14 ng/mL: active, confirmed [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.10" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>First prenatal visit: blood count, ferritin, quantitative hCG, blood group and antibody screen, rubella immunity, hepatitis B surface antigen, HIV, syphilis, and hepatitis C tests; urine culture; influenza vaccine; prenatal vitamin with folic acid. Guideline: USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Guidelines for Vaccinating Pregnant Persons (2026) [S]</item><item>Maternal-fetal medicine consultation with a first-trimester ultrasound at 11 weeks for a uterus large for dates: dating, the number of fetuses and, if more than one, chorionicity; nuchal translucency; and fibroids or a molar pregnancy. Guideline: Multifetal Gestations: Twin, Triplet, and Higher-Order Multifetal Pregnancies: ACOG Practice Bulletin, Number 231 (2021); Committee Opinion No 700: Methods for Estimating the Due Date (2017) [S]</item><item>Nausea and vomiting: small, frequent, bland meals, ginger, and doxylamine with pyridoxine at bedtime; return for vomiting that stops her keeping fluids down, weight loss, or dizziness. Guideline: ACOG Practice Bulletin No. 189: Nausea and Vomiting of Pregnancy (2018) [S]</item><item>Iron deficiency anemia: ferrous sulfate 325 mg every other day; blood count and ferritin at the anatomy-scan visit, with intravenous iron in the second trimester if there is no response. Guideline: Anemia in Pregnancy: ACOG Practice Bulletin, Number 233 (2021) [S]</item><item>Mood: EPDS in each trimester and after the birth. Guideline: Screening and Diagnosis of Mental Health Conditions During Pregnancy and Postpartum: ACOG Clinical Practice Guideline No. 4 (2023) [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
</component>
